# ⚙️ Laravel 12 Product API Project Configuration

<project_context>
- The project is built using Laravel 12 with PHP 8.3+.
- The database used is PostgreSQL.
- The application is a RESTful API managing products.
- The main model is `Product` with fields: id (auto-increment), name (string), price (float), created_at, updated_at.
</project_context>

<coding_guidelines>
- Use Eloquent ORM for all model interactions.
- Always define `$fillable` properties in models to allow mass assignment.
- Follow the "Fat Models, Skinny Controllers" approach — put business logic in the model, keep controllers simple.
- Apply validation using `request()->validate()` inside controllers or create dedicated Form Request classes.
- Use RESTful conventions in routing and resource controllers.
- Use eager loading (`with()`) when accessing related models to avoid N+1 query issues.
- Use Laravel Resources (`Http\Resources`) for formatting API responses.
- Use route model binding for cleaner and more readable code.
- Always write PHPUnit tests using `RefreshDatabase` for a clean state.
- Migrate database structure via Artisan commands and version control migrations.

